(* README *)

1 - Summary
    -------

    P001 formalizes the following finite divisibility statement:
    among any `n + 1` pairwise distinct positive integers chosen from
    `1` through `2n`, there exist two distinct selected integers such
    that one divides the other.

    The mathematical proof is the standard pigeonhole argument. The package
    also demonstrates constructive multiplexing: several proof presentations
    are named explicitly, while one completed realization is selected by a
    small switch and exported to the terminal theorem.

    Terminal artifact:

      `pigeonhole_divisibility_qed : WITNESS`

2 - State
    -----

    Closed formalization of a standard pigeonhole divisibility theorem.


3 - Intuition
    ---------

    The proof uses the usual pigeonhole-divisibility idea. Each selected
    integer is written as a power of two times an odd part. There are only `n`
    possible odd parts in the interval `1` through `2n`, so choosing `n + 1`
    distinct integers forces two of them to share the same odd part. The one
    with the smaller power of two then divides the one with the larger power.

    The constructive multiplexing layout presents this standard proof in five
    layers:

      - Contract: the theorem statement.
      - Reframing: a semantic packaging of the problem.
      - Multiplexed presentations: explicit named proof presentations.
      - Switch: the selected completed realization.
      - QED: the terminal certification theorem.

    The method makes the proof history visible without changing the final
    statement being certified.


4 - Tree
    ----

    Stdlib
     ▼
    P001_00_Premises
     ▼
    P001_01__Reframing
     ▼
    P001_98_Multiplexing/*
     ▼
    P001_98_98__Switch
     ▼
    P001_98_QED
     ▼
    P001_99_Artifacts


5 - Files
    -----

    P001_00_Premises.v

      Contract layer. Defines `PROPOSITIO` and `WITNESS`.

    P001_01__Reframing.v

      Semantic expansion layer. Packages the target into smaller
      components and proves that the reframed statement implies
      `WITNESS`.

    P001_98_Multiplexing/P001_98_01A__Initial.v

      Conjectural historical initial presentation of the target proof
      obligation. It is recorded as part of the multiplexing history, but it is
      not the terminal proof selected by the switch.

    P001_98_Multiplexing/P001_98_01B__Expansion.v

      Conjectural historical expansion presentation. It reuses the canonical
      `first_expansion` shape from `P001_01__Reframing` and records that a proof
      of that expansion would imply `WITNESS`; it is not the terminal proof
      selected by the switch.

    P001_98_Multiplexing/P001_98_02A__Peeling.v

      Names the four mathematical obligations used by the proof. This is the
      shared peeled-obligation shape reused by the completed proof layer.

    P001_98_Multiplexing/P001_98_02B__Rewrite.v

      Conjectural historical rewrite presentation. It assembles four named
      obligations into the proof witness, but the terminal switch does not
      select this layer.

    P001_98_Multiplexing/P001_98_02C__Proof.v

      Completed proof. Proves the peeled obligations and exports
      `UNCONDITIONAL_PROOF : WITNESS`.

    P001_98_Multiplexing/P001_98_98__Switch.v

      Constructive switch. Selects the completed proof realization exported to
      the terminal theorem.

    P001_98_QED.v

      Terminal certification layer. Proves
      `pigeonhole_divisibility_qed : WITNESS`
      from the selected proof witness.

    P001_99_Artifacts.v

      Artifact layer. Records the `Print Assumptions` report for the terminal
      theorem.

    _appendix/_assumptions/

      `Print Assumptions` output for the terminal theorem.


6 - API
    ---

    Recommended imports:

      Contract only:
        `From P001 Require Import P001_00_Premises.`

      Certified endpoint:
        `From P001 Require Import P001_98_QED.`

    Public contract:

      PROPOSITIO   : Prop
      WITNESS      : Prop

    Certified endpoint:

      pigeonhole_divisibility_qed : WITNESS

    Selected proof witness:

      UNCONDITIONAL_PROOF : WITNESS


7 - Notes
    -----

    The switch selects:

      `P001_98_Multiplexing/P001_98_02C__Proof.v`

    and the terminal theorem is closed under the global context in the
    recorded `Print Assumptions` output.
